{"id": "EUVD-2026-82067", "enisaUuid": "68ef4381-e64a-39ef-b4c9-25037e5425ed", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: qcom: iris: handle runtime PM resume failure in core deinit\n\nCheck the return value of pm_runtime_resume_and_get() in\niris_core_deinit().\n\nIf runtime PM resume fails, skip hardware power-off operations but\nstill perform software teardown and state transition. Also skip the\ncorresponding pm_runtime_put_sync() call to avoid unbalanced runtime\nPM references.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:09:34", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:03:10", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e7768f3dae9f2c6e5b80e9c02429550ea39f2be6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cb83cfff8dff5d546fadce15596e01b1504b632a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/75d79879ec3cbfd288144b0ae4c3e3fa7700c5fc"], "aliases": ["GHSA-gx53-gmpj-4j7w", "CVE-2026-90406"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "11d4d14f-e0ab-36a3-a1d6-f3312a69b7d8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "3a9ef3b9-11ad-3b9f-a668-fd97b7ccf17f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bb8a95aa038e099f5ec82c466e996b006e05abd7 <75d79879ec3cbfd288144b0ae4c3e3fa7700c5fc"}, {"id": "4f37a9f4-df6f-31be-8145-39f1d3114ab9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "6334505d-4a77-31a4-80e5-07abd34671e4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "d2b00d2b-2e70-37ca-ae4c-dbea43dac8e8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bb8a95aa038e099f5ec82c466e996b006e05abd7 <e7768f3dae9f2c6e5b80e9c02429550ea39f2be6"}, {"id": "e11338b5-3940-337c-b0a4-c3244e94a984", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.15"}, {"id": "f123940a-5934-37aa-8233